  "biobricks:reviewed": false,
  "biobricks:reviewNotes": "Determined by the BioBricks licensing-provenance annotation agent (Claude). The brick scrapes the NIEHS/NTP CEBS resource (cebs-ext.niehs.nih.gov). CEBS is produced by the U.S. National Toxicology Program, a federal program; NTP's own web policy states its information is in the public domain and may be copied and distributed without permission (citation appreciated). Classed open / US Government Work with commercial use permitted. HUMAN REVIEW: confirm none of the ~47 scraped datasets carry an explicit third-party copyright notice, and note that SMILES were backfilled from a local DSSTox (EPA CompTox) table, which is itself US-Government / public-domain.",
